    {
      "heading": "Operators",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "content": "Operators are used to perform operations on variables and values."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "content": "In the example below, we use the `+` **operator** to add together two values:"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "content": "  int myNum = 100 + 50;"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "content": "Although the `+` operator is often used to add together two values, like in the example above, it can also be used to add together a variable and a value, or a variable and another variable:"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "content": "  int sum1 = 100 + 50;        \n  // 150 (100 + 50)\n\n  int sum2 = sum1 + 250;      // 400 (150 + 250)\n\n  int sum3 = sum2 + sum2;     // 800 (400 + 400)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "content": "C divides the operators into the following groups:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "Arithmetic operators",
            "Assignment operators",
            "Comparison operators",
            "Logical operators",
            "Bitwise operators (advanced)"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
